HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_3732bbc, "`owned <freer>` says C writes a string THROUGH this cell and the compiler frees it with that function, so it belongs on a `@x: cstr` out-parameter or on a `cstr` result. On anything else it says nothing the compiler can act on");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_4eb44276, "no extern declares it");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_7df95e0, "unknown_freer");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_708d9dc, "` frees nothing here: no `extern` in this module declares it, so `owned ");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_69bca327, "` names a function the compiler cannot call");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_684a6265, "` is a Heroes function in this program; a freer is the C function that owns the allocation, declared in a group");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_71a9f026, "declare `function ");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_6ba05600, "(p: ptr)` in a group of this module \342\200\224 the header that group names is what clang checks the freer against");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_638e4f74, "\302\2474.19: the compiler frees an `owned` string by calling the freer by name, so the name has to be one this module's headers know");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_75651389, "freer_arity");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_b55ab14, "` takes ");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_6021ae94, " parameters, and a freer for an `owned` string is handed exactly one: the string");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_15437021, "name the function that frees THIS string \342\200\224 `free` for `strdup`, `sqlite3_free` for SQLite's own \342\200\224 or drop the `owned ");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_54d1314d, "` mark and free it yourself");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_dc6a322, "fine");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_2687966e, "a one-parameter extern of this module");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_37b4f297, "owned_freer_called");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_3c789acd, "` is what frees an `owned` string in this program, so the compiler already calls it \342\200\224 calling it here frees the string twice");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_17338d7, "the `owned ");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_7ae3c839, "` that says so is ");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_62a1a65, "\302\2474.19: a marked string is handed over as a `str?`, already copied \342\200\224 the bytes C gave you are gone by the time you hold it");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_3f3ff731, "delete this call and let the compiler free it, or delete the `owned ");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_282a7421, "release");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_2dfda7a5, "expected `");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_7a5d94f6, "`, found `");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_25d7e1cf, "` takes two of one type \342\200\224 two integers of the SAME width, or two floats of the same width \342\200\224 and found `");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_733e5991, "one side is text, so no `to_<width>` can help \342\200\224 those answer a number, and `+` on a `str` wants a `str`. Render the other side: `\"n is \" + n.to_str()`");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_533204fc, "convert one side: `to_f64(x)` cannot fail, and `to_i64(x)` or another `to_<width>(x)` gives a `T?` because the number may not fit");
